            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Exactly like the Hummingbirds in Jamaica. Hint: for the Strawberry syrup, you can use one found with the pancake syrups."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "BMaples"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Nice flavor, a little too sweet with too little of a kick for my taste. For all of you saying that you cannot find Rum cream it's basically RumChata which is an excellent substitute.",
            "datePublished": "2016-03-01T05:20:14.523Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Curt"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is it.. like Montego Bay! :) We don't like the coffee flavor as much, so we use amaretto. Sometimes I also use 1 oz strawberry liqueur in place of the strawberry syrup for a little more kick, and a little less strawberry flavor, but that's less authentic. BTW, to those making this with rum.. definitely not the same... We bring lots of rum creme back from jamaica, but Cruzan now distributes a rum creme in the US now, I have a bottle, but haven't run out of Sangster's yet.. :) I'll update when I do..",
            "datePublished": "2010-03-03T16:21:21.110Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SmokeysMom"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I could not find any rum cream, so used straight rum. This did not taste at all like the Hummingbird I drank often at Breezes Runaway Bay, and I don't think its because of what I substituted (rum for rum cream).\n\nWhat I did do, since I tasted the coffee liqueur, is I added another ounce of milk, and another ounce of strawberry flavored syrup. THAT tasted more like the drink I had, though it wasn't the same color (mine was brownish instead of pink).\n\nSo this is a nice recipe, but I had to modify it a little.",
            "datePublished": "2008-07-13T12:49:52.543Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "sephira95"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe definitely makes me want to go to Jamaica! I used Rum Chata cream rum. It was pretty easy to find. This is a must try!",
            "datePublished": "2013-05-08T15:47:11.823Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SouthernFriedFun"
            },
            "reviewBody": "For those that may not know, Tia Maria is the preferred coffee flavored liqueur used ! We always bring home a couple of bottle of Jamaican rum cream each year when we go. Cruzan is a Puerto Rican rum and just not the same as Jamaican Rum ( cream or otherwise!! )",
            "datePublished": "2010-09-20T12:18:15.830Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Exactly like the ones we had in the Bahamas on our honeymoon. One difference, instead of rum cream liquor they just used Bacardi rum, you can use a flavored version for extra fruity taste. We like to add more banana to the mix. Love them, perfect for hot summer days or pool parties.",
            "datePublished": "2008-01-21T08:48:09.580Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "DiamondGirl amanecer"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I`ve already rated this recipe. I made it with white rum, but now I made it with Rum Cream liqueur. I bought it in Dominican Republic and really fell in love with its taste. The cocktail is extremely good, not strong at all, the ingredients perfectly compliment each other. Using rum, the taste will be a little different, but good.",
            "datePublished": "2008-05-12T03:41:48.253Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Bonnie, PA"
            },
            "reviewBody": "HAVING BEEN TO JAMAICA 3 TIMES, THIS IS OUR FIRST DRINK REQUEST EVERY TIME. IT IS EXCELLENT!! I PUT ONLY 1/2 OUNCE OF THE COFFEE LIQUER IN, BUT STILL GREAT!!\nLAST TIME THERE, I BOUGHT THE COCONUT RUM CREAM AND THERE'S HARDLY ANY DIFFERENCE. STILL TERRIFIC! FILLING BUT A GREAT DESSERT DRINK!!",
            "datePublished": "2008-06-06T08:41:36.663Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Zippy"
            },
            "reviewBody": "FABULOUS! I used gold rum and half &amp; half in place of the rum cream liqueor and milk. I added a little extra syrup and kahlua. It seems like a strange combination, but ohhhh.... they were yummy.",
            "datePublished": "2006-11-10T15:33:50.397Z"
          },
